From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:10:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mix.json: the ground sound thread's land block of 19:09Z (two
 German MG stretches; pooled players, off)

land.mgClose.moreParts gains mg42_burst_01 [[0.31, 1.19], [0.5, 1.19]] and
mg42_burst_02 [[0.19, 0.59]], measured from each take's rounds, so a crowded
German MG plays another stretch of firing instead of a copy (the Kursk
fault); the _moreParts note says so. New land.voices (pool false, warm 256,
most 384): the ground battle's pooled players, off until the 3D pre-check
and a Mac sound-on comparison pass, so nothing in the game changes yet.
The land block now equals sound/mix/land-block.json (ground thread's branch
claude/project-thread-ixbnpu at 6900aad1). Nothing in the air block changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
